---
/**
 * The two-layer picture that the whole project rests on.
 *
 * The Jekyll site drew this as ASCII art inside a <pre>. That reads well in a
 * terminal and badly on a phone, where it either wraps into nonsense or forces
 * a horizontal scroll. This is the same diagram in flowing markup: it reflows,
 * it can be read aloud in order, and it takes the page's own colours.
 */
---

<div class="arch">
  <section class="arch-node" aria-labelledby="arch-phone">
    <p class="arch-kicker">Always</p>
    <h3 id="arch-phone">iPhone — the Helsa app</h3>
    <p class="arch-flow"><span>HealthKit</span><span>analysis</span><span>what you see</span></p>
    <p class="arch-note">
      HealthKit is the store and the analysis runs on the device. This works
      fully offline, with no server at all.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="arch-link" role="presentation">
    <span class="arch-line"></span>
    <p>
      <strong>Optional, opt-in, and you type the URL.</strong>{' '}
      Mutual TLS plus a device token.
    </p>
    <span class="arch-line"></span>
  </div>

  <section class="arch-node arch-node--server" aria-labelledby="arch-server">
    <p class="arch-kicker">Only if you want it</p>
    <h3 id="arch-server">Your server — this repository</h3>
    <p class="arch-flow">
      <span>Caddy</span><span>API</span><span>RabbitMQ</span><span>worker</span><span>TimescaleDB</span>
    </p>
    <p class="arch-note">
      Long-term history, a web dashboard on your LAN or VPN, exports, and daily
      summaries for Home Assistant.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="arch-caption">
    The phone is the <strong>only writer</strong>. Every other surface — the web
    dashboard, an iPad, Home Assistant — reads from the server. That asymmetry is
    not a preference: HealthKit has no cloud API, so the device holding the data
    is the only thing that can upload it.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .arch {
    margin-top: 2.4rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .arch-node {
    border: 1px solid var(--helsa-border);
    border-radius: var(--helsa-radius);
    background: var(--helsa-surface);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* An aurora edge marks the layer that is always present; the server layer
     gets a plain edge, because it is the optional one. */
  .arch-node::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-block: 0;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    width: 3px;
    background: var(--helsa-aurora);
  }
  .arch-node--server::before { background: var(--helsa-border-strong); }

  .arch-kicker {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--helsa-ink-faint);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .arch-node h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; }

  .arch-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0.85rem;
    font-family: var(--helsa-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.83rem;
  }
  .arch-flow span {
    border: 1px solid var(--helsa-border);
    background: var(--helsa-bg-sunken);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem;
    color: var(--helsa-ink);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* The arrows are decoration between the stages, so they are generated rather
     than written into the markup where a screen reader would announce them. */
  .arch-flow span + span::before {
    content: '→';
    color: var(--helsa-ink-faint);
    margin-inline-end: 0.55rem;
    margin-inline-start: -0.15rem;
  }

  .arch-note {
    color: var(--helsa-ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .arch-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding-block: 0.9rem;
  }
  .arch-link p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.87rem;
    color: var(--helsa-ink-muted);
    text-align: center;
    flex: none;
    max-width: 26rem;
  }
  .arch-link strong { color: var(--helsa-ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .arch-line {
    flex: 1;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--helsa-border-strong));
  }
  .arch-link .arch-line:last-child {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--helsa-border-strong), transparent);
  }

  .arch-caption {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--helsa-ink-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .arch-caption strong { color: var(--helsa-ink); }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .arch-link { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
    .arch-line { width: 1px; height: 1.1rem; flex: none; background: var(--helsa-border-strong); }
    .arch-link .arch-line:last-child { background: var(--helsa-border-strong); }
  }
</style>
